# Shell scripts MUST keep LF line endings. A CRLF shebang fails inside Linux
# containers with `env: 'bash\r': No such file or directory`, so a Windows
# checkout (autocrlf) that rewrites run.sh to CRLF would make a locally-built
# image (add-on or `docker compose up --build`) refuse to boot. These attributes
# override core.autocrlf for matched files on every platform.
*.sh text eol=lf
addon/run.sh text eol=lf

# Docker build assets are consumed in Linux: keep them LF so a Windows checkout
# can't introduce CRLF (a trailing \r in a .dockerignore pattern stops it
# matching; CRLF in a Dockerfile can break RUN heredocs/line continuations).
.dockerignore text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.dockerfile text eol=lf

# index.html carries an inline theme <script> whose sha256 is pinned in the
# backend Content-Security-Policy (main.py). A Windows checkout that rewrites it
# to CRLF changes the hash, so a locally-built image serves a script the CSP
# rejects (a stale open tab then shows a scary CSP error after a rebuild).
# Browsers normalise CRLF->LF so a fresh load is fine, but lock it to LF anyway
# to match the Linux/prod build the hash is computed against.
frontend/index.html text eol=lf

# Binary assets — never normalise line endings (would corrupt them).
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
